Z||000003||WampusCat||12-04-2001||07:22 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007662.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007662.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010824-2-008170.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010824-2-008170.html</A> <P>I got one off of E-bay for $180.  Works great, red lights match the dash, not too hard to install.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-04-2001||08:17 AM||||They are kind of expensive but at the below link you can buy a referbished one. If you find one somewhere else (Ebay, Junkyard, Etc)<BR>the below link sells the harness adapters to plug-in the newer GM stereo's.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mnrelectronics.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mnrelectronics.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||12-04-2001||08:55 AM||||I got one from the link Oreif posted, just like the one pictured in the first post. The part# is 16205302. <BR>Got the wiring adapter there, too. It's *not* cheap, but the advantage of buying here over buying from E-bay is the warranty.<BR>I also *love* mine. If you don't have a subwoofer, I'd highly recommend Pioneer TSA-4103s for the dash. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Toogy||12-04-2001||11:03 AM||||What year of pontiac CD player will fit easily into a Fiero?  Will any GM Delco CD Player work?  Anybody know?<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR><B>Soon to be: 1987 GT 5-speed</B>||||reg||1
Z||000007||RRobinson||12-04-2001||12:34 PM||||I have Delco/Pontiac CD players in 4 of my Fieros. I got most of them through Ebay. The most recent cost me $150US and was brand new manufactured in June/01.<BR> <BR>I love the sound and love the look. The grey buttons and red lighting match the Fiero interior perfectly. I would recommend them to anyone.<P>RR<BR>88 GT 5.5K Bone stock<BR>88 GT 40K w/CD<BR>87 GT 15K w/CD<BR>87 GT 55K w/CD<BR>87 SE V6 <BR>86 GT 41K w/CD<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Toogy||12-04-2001||12:37 PM||||So any year Delco/Pontiac CD player will work?  How much work is involved?<P>Details please.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||12-04-2001||02:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Toogy:<BR><B>So any year Delco/Pontiac CD player will work?  How much work is involved?<P>Details please.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Any year of the large face GM stereo's will work. You just need the adapter harness. See website I posted above. It will show different stereo's and what year/vehicle they came from. That way you can search for used ones for a particular year and car to get what you want. <BR>Work is easy. Pull out old radio, plug in harness adapter, plug in new stereo, Done!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
